      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 57.39,
      "end_seconds": 61.28,
      "duration_seconds": 3.89,
      "text": "Have you had any red eyes or vomiting?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 61.85,
      "end_seconds": 65.97,
      "duration_seconds": 4.12,
      "text": "so no red eyes or vomiting none of it"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 66.94,
      "end_seconds": 71.46,
      "duration_seconds": 4.52,
      "text": "Let me check a few things. Any cough or bleeding?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 72.38,
      "end_seconds": 75.79,
      "duration_seconds": 3.41,
      "text": "right, no, no cough or bleeding"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 76.91,
      "end_seconds": 78.5,
      "duration_seconds": 1.59,
      "text": "how's your breathing otherwise?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 80.12,
      "end_seconds": 82.71,
      "duration_seconds": 2.59,
      "text": "no, my breathing's been fine"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 97.16,
      "end_seconds": 102.04,
      "duration_seconds": 4.88,
      "text": "tell me about your routine, work, habits, that sort of thing"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 103.16,
      "end_seconds": 116.48,
      "duration_seconds": 13.32,
      "text": "I'm a software engineer, so I'm at a screen all day. Barely, I'm mostly sedentary these days. Yes, I live on my own."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 117.21,
      "end_seconds": 121.05,
      "duration_seconds": 3.84,
      "text": "Do your parents or siblings have any long-term illnesses?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 122.28,
      "end_seconds": 126.03,
      "duration_seconds": 3.75,
      "text": "my father had a a heart attack"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 128.05,
      "end_seconds": 133.32,
      "duration_seconds": 5.27,
      "text": "What about your general health, any conditions you're being treated for?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 136.28,
      "end_seconds": 140.1,
      "duration_seconds": 3.82,
      "text": "High blood pressure, for nearly five years"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 153.01,
      "end_seconds": 154.25,
      "duration_seconds": 1.24,
      "text": "Any previous surgeries?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 155.56,
      "end_seconds": 161.8,
      "duration_seconds": 6.24,
      "text": "right, I had my thyroid operated on a long time ago"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 162.77,
      "end_seconds": 165.12,
      "duration_seconds": 2.35,
      "text": "Any allergies I should know about?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 166.41,
      "end_seconds": 173.18,
      "duration_seconds": 6.77,
      "text": "years back I got hives from penicillin, so I stay away from it now"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 174.57,
      "end_seconds": 178.62,
      "duration_seconds": 4.05,
      "text": "Any medication at the moment, including things from the pharmacy?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 180.5,
      "end_seconds": 186.59,
      "duration_seconds": 6.09,
      "text": "I take ramipril, 5 milligrams, every morning for my blood pressure"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 187.64,
      "end_seconds": 190.79,
      "duration_seconds": 3.15,
      "text": "Before we go on a few quick readings."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 200.76,
      "end_seconds": 202.41,
      "duration_seconds": 1.65,
      "text": "Hold still for me..."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 211.72,
      "end_seconds": 218.46,
      "duration_seconds": 6.74,
      "text": "Okay: pressure 115 over 74, SpO2 95 percent on room air, temperature 38.4, pulse 101."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 221.11,
      "end_seconds": 224.14,
      "duration_seconds": 3.03,
      "text": "Alright, shall we do the examination?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 225.25,
      "end_seconds": 227.44,
      "duration_seconds": 2.19,
      "text": "take your time, no rush"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 244.56,
      "end_seconds": 249.78,
      "duration_seconds": 5.22,
      "text": "A fine rash over the chest and back not itchy to touch."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 254.69,
      "end_seconds": 275.21,
      "duration_seconds": 20.52,
      "text": "Thanks for that. Okay so my impression is this: The most likely explanation is a viral fever with joint involvement, possibly chikungunya. The reason I say that is that your story and my examination fit together. I can't rule out an early inflammatory arthritis yet."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 277.17,
      "end_seconds": 280.74,
      "duration_seconds": 3.57,
      "text": "what are the chances it's something bad?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 281.48,
      "end_seconds": 293.01,
      "duration_seconds": 11.53,
      "text": "I understand the worry. At the moment I'd say it's a viral fever with joint involvement, possibly chikungunya, and we'll know more once the a dengue test is back"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 306.32,
      "end_seconds": 325.19,
      "duration_seconds": 18.87,
      "text": "I want a dengue test done, that's for fever. I'll start you on paracetamol, 650 milligrams, three times a day, for five days. It's for fever and joint pain. Avoid anti-inflammatory painkillers until we know it it isn't dengue. Alright, I'll see you out."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 326.16,
      "end_seconds": 331.57,
      "duration_seconds": 5.41,
      "text": "hmm, that's everything I wanted to ask thank you"
    }
  ]
